---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';

const toc = [
  { id: 'setup',      label: 'Set up the keyboard' },
  { id: 'dictate',    label: 'How to dictate' },
  { id: 'full-access', label: 'Why Full Access' },
  { id: 'data',       label: 'Your data' },
  { id: 'troubleshooting', label: 'Troubleshooting' },
  { id: 'contact',    label: 'Contact' },
];

const title = 'Support — Rekody';
const description = 'How to set up and use the Rekody keyboard for iPhone, plus answers to common questions.';
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <LegalPage
    eyebrow="Support"
    title="Help with Rekody."
    updated="July 8, 2026"
    summary="Rekody is a voice keyboard for iPhone. Speak, and it types the words where your cursor is. Everything runs on your device."
    toc={toc}
  >
    <section id="setup">
      <h2>Set up the keyboard</h2>
      <p>Two things turn Rekody on. The app walks you through both the first time you open it.</p>
      <ol>
        <li>Open <strong>Settings › General › Keyboard › Keyboards › Add New Keyboard</strong> and choose <strong>Rekody</strong>.</li>
        <li>Tap <strong>Rekody</strong> in that list and turn on <strong>Allow Full Access</strong>.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        Now in any app, tap the globe on your keyboard to switch to Rekody. You'll see the teal talk bar.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="dictate">
      <h2>How to dictate</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Tap the teal <strong>talk bar</strong>. Rekody opens and starts listening.</li>
        <li>Speak. Your words appear live as you talk.</li>
        <li>Stop talking, or tap <strong>Stop</strong>. Rekody finishes on its own after a short pause.</li>
        <li>Go back to your app. Rekody types the text the moment the keyboard returns.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        You can glance back to your app while you're still talking. The live words follow you in the Dynamic
        Island and the keyboard bar, and you can stop right from there.
      </p>
      <div class="callout">
        <p>
          The first time you dictate, Rekody downloads the on-device voice model, about 1.1 GB. Stay on Wi-Fi
          for that one download. After that, dictation works fully offline.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="full-access">
      <h2>Why Full Access</h2>
      <p>
        iOS only lets a keyboard place text into another app once you turn on <strong>Allow Full Access</strong>.
        Rekody uses it for exactly that. It does not send your audio or your words anywhere, because Rekody has
        no server to send them to. Everything happens on your iPhone.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="data">
      <h2>Your data</h2>
      <p>
        Your audio never leaves your iPhone. Your dictation history is stored locally in the app, and you can
        delete any entry, or all of them, at any time. There are no accounts and no tracking. For the full
        picture, see the <a href="/privacy">privacy page</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="troubleshooting">
      <h2>Troubleshooting</h2>
      <h3>The text didn't get typed</h3>
      <p>
        Make sure <strong>Allow Full Access</strong> is on for Rekody in Settings › General › Keyboard ›
        Keyboards › Rekody. Without it, iOS blocks the keyboard from placing text.
      </p>
      <h3>Rekody won't record</h3>
      <p>
        Check that microphone access is on in <strong>Settings › Rekody</strong>. The app shows a reminder if
        it's off.
      </p>
      <h3>The talk bar is greyed out</h3>
      <p>
        Rekody turns itself off in password and other secure fields on purpose. Switch to a normal text field
        and it comes back.
      </p>
      <h3>Dictation seems stuck the first time</h3>
      <p>
        That's the one-time model download finishing. Keep the app open on Wi-Fi. Your words are captured while
        it loads, so nothing you say is lost.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="contact">
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Email <a href="mailto:support@rekody.com">support@rekody.com</a>. Tell us your iPhone model and iOS
        version and we'll help.
      </p>
    </section>
  </LegalPage>
</Base>
